From: Mira <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: 2026-10-07
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: recognise the Pi's SAND column formats

The Raspberry Pi 4's HEVC decoder (rpivid, /dev/video19) offers exactly two
capture formats, NC12 and NC30 - Broadcom's SAND layout. GStreamer knows
neither, so gst_v4l2_decoder_enum_src_formats returns EMPTY caps and the
plugin logs

    Found decoder device rpi-hevc-dec-proc
    Registering rpi-hevc-dec-proc as H265 Decoder
    Not registering H265 decoder since it produces no supported format

leaving the Pi with no hardware HEVC path at all. Measured on the box with
VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT: the capture queue offers NC12 and NC30 and nothing else,
before or after setting the coded format, while /dev/video10 (H.264) offers
plain NV12 - which is exactly why H.264 works here and HEVC does not.

Map them to the linear formats with the same sample layout. Buffer size and
stride already come from the driver's sizeimage/bytesperline, so the linear
geometry is never used to size anything; the memory layout only matters to a
consumer that reads the pixels, and on this box the buffers go to the GPU as
dmabufs, which can sample SAND when imported with the matching DRM modifier.

Upstream would want a real GstVideoFormat for the column layout; this is the
smaller change that makes the hardware reachable.

Signed-off-by: Mira <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2format.c	2026-10-07 21:05:59.549411594 +0200
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2format.c	2026-10-07 22:45:17.186246219 +0200
@@ -31,6 +31,32 @@
   gint subsampling;
 };
 
+/*
+ * The Raspberry Pi's HEVC decoder (rpivid, /dev/video19) only ever offers
+ * these two capture formats - Broadcom's SAND layout, where the image is cut
+ * into 128-byte wide columns rather than stored line by line. They are not in
+ * any mainline header, so define them here.
+ */
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128 v4l2_fourcc('N', 'C', '1', '2')
+#endif
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_10_COL128
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_10_COL128 v4l2_fourcc('N', 'C', '3', '0')
+#endif
+/*
+ * ...and their two-plane twins, which is what the driver actually hands back.
+ * Asked for plain NV12 it substitutes 'Nc12' - the same SAND layout with Y and
+ * UV as separate planes - and a decoder whose returned format is not in this
+ * table fails negotiation with "Unsupported bitdepth/chroma format", which is
+ * what happened before these were added (measured on the box, 2026-10-07).
+ */
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_COL128
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_COL128 v4l2_fourcc('N', 'c', '1', '2')
+#endif
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_10_COL128
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_10_COL128 v4l2_fourcc('N', 'c', '3', '0')
+#endif
+
 static struct FormatEntry format_map[] = {
   {V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12, 1, GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_NV12, 8, 420},
   {V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUYV, 1, GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_YUY2, 8, 422},
@@ -42,6 +68,32 @@
   {V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV15_4L4, 1, GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_NV12_10LE40_4L4, 10, 420},
   {V4L2_PIX_FMT_MT2110T, 2, GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_MT2110T, 10, 420},
   {V4L2_PIX_FMT_MT2110R, 2, GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_MT2110R, 10, 420},
+  /*
+   * Mira: the Pi's SAND column formats, carried as their linear equivalents.
+   *
+   * Without these the plugin finds rpi-hevc-dec, gets EMPTY capture caps and
+   * logs "Not registering H265 decoder since it produces no supported
+   * format" - so the Pi's HEVC decoder is simply absent from GStreamer, and
+   * every HEVC title has to be transcoded by the server.
+   *
+   * The sample layout within a plane is the same as NV12 (and as the 32-bit
+   * packed 10-bit variant); what differs is how the planes are arranged in
+   * memory, which only matters to whoever reads the pixels. Nothing on the
+   * CPU does: the buffers are dmabufs handed to the GPU, and V3D can sample
+   * SAND directly when the image is imported with
+   * DRM_FORMAT_MOD_BROADCOM_SAND128 (see v3d_resource.c - NV12 exposes
+   * LINEAR, UIF and SAND128; P030 exposes SAND128 alone). The importer must
+   * therefore apply that modifier; with LINEAR the picture decodes but comes
+   * out scrambled into columns, which is the symptom to expect if this is
+   * half-done.
+   *
+   * Size and stride come from the driver's own sizeimage/bytesperline below,
+   * so the wrong linear geometry is never used to size a buffer.
+   */
+  {V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128, 1, GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_NV12, 8, 420},
+  {V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_10_COL128, 1, GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_NV12_10LE32, 10, 420},
+  {V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_COL128, 2, GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_NV12, 8, 420},
+  {V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_10_COL128, 2, GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_NV12_10LE32, 10, 420},
   {0,}
 };
 
--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2format.h	2026-10-07 21:05:59.550029452 +0200
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2format.h	2026-10-07 21:05:59.564656305 +0200
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 #include "linux/videodev2.h"
 
 #define GST_V4L2_DEFAULT_VIDEO_FORMATS "{ " \
-  "P010_10LE, NV12_10LE40_4L4, MT2110T, MT2110R," \
+  "P010_10LE, NV12_10LE40_4L4, MT2110T, MT2110R, NV12_10LE32," \
   "NV12, YUY2, NV12_4L4, NV12_32L32, NV12_16L32S, I420" \
   "}"
 
